<section id="cx-sources" class="cx-section-sources">
  <div class="cx-wrap">
    <div class="cx-kicker">Check the facts</div>
    <h2 class="cx-title">Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <p class="cx-lede">Every figure on this page, with its source. If you spot something wrong, tell us and we'll fix it.</p>
    <ol class="cx-src-list">
<li id="cx-src-1"><span class="cx-src-num">1</span><div><p>Mines in the Gardens of Stone region remove more than 20 billion litres of groundwater every year. Also stated by Chris Jonkers in Watershed, Episode 1.</p><p class="cx-src-links"><a href="https://assets.nationbuilder.com/natureorg/pages/4621/attachments/original/1738293846/Centennial_Coal_Report_FINAL.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nature Conservation Council of NSW, environmental scorecard (PDF, January 2025)</a></p></div></li>
<li id="cx-src-2"><span class="cx-src-num">2</span><div><p>Mine water inflows currently represent 80 to 90 per cent of Coxs River baseflows. Lithgow Environment Group's own submission.</p><p class="cx-src-links"><a href="https://www.lithgowenvironment.au/docs/submissions/leg-project-officer-submission-lake-lyell-pumped-hydro.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEG submission, Lake Lyell pumped hydro project (PDF)</a></p></div></li>
